  "body": "## Summary\nThe Ekubo Router contract does not include a deadline parameter in any of its swap functions, unlike industry-standard DEX routers (Uniswap V2/V3, Curve, etc.). This allows transactions to execute at any point in the future as long as slippage requirements are met, potentially resulting in unwanted trade execution when user intent has changed.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe Router contract's swap functions lack a deadline parameter and corresponding `block.timestamp` check:\n\n**Links to affected code:**\n- https://github.com/code-423n4/2025-11-ekubo/blob/main/src/Router.sol#L266-L272\n- https://github.com/code-423n4/2025-11-ekubo/blob/main/src/Router.sol#L280-L289\n- https://github.com/code-423n4/2025-11-ekubo/blob/main/src/Router.sol#L300-L317\n- https://github.com/code-423n4/2025-11-ekubo/blob/main/src/Router.sol#L327-L338\n- https://github.com/code-423n4/2025-11-ekubo/blob/main/src/Router.sol#L347-L353\n- https://github.com/code-423n4/2025-11-ekubo/blob/main/src/Router.sol#L380-L388\n- https://github.com/code-423n4/2025-11-ekubo/blob/main/src/Router.sol#L394-L403\n\n## Vulnerability Details\n\n### The Issue\nAll swap functions in Router.sol accept slippage protection (`calculatedAmountThreshold`) but none accept a deadline parameter. This means:\n\n1. A user submits a swap transaction at time T1\n2. The transaction sits in the mempool (due to low gas, network congestion, etc.)\n3. At time T2 (hours/days/weeks later), the user's intent may have changed\n4. The transaction can still execute as long as slippage requirements are met\n5. User receives tokens they no longer want/need\n\n### Comparison with Industry Standard\n\n**Uniswap V2 Router:**\n```solidity\nfunction swapExactTokensForTokens(\n    uint amountIn,\n    uint amountOutMin,\n    address[] calldata path,\n    address to,\n    uint deadline  // ← Deadline parameter\n) external returns (uint[] memory amounts) {\n    require(deadline >= block.timestamp, 'UniswapV2Router: EXPIRED');\n    // ...\n}\n```\n\n**Ekubo Router:**\n```solidity\nfunction swap(\n    PoolKey memory poolKey, \n    SwapParameters params, \n    int256 calculatedAmountThreshold  // ← Only slippage, NO deadline\n) public payable returns (PoolBalanceUpdate balanceUpdate)\n```\n\n### Key Distinction: Slippage vs Deadline\n\n| Protection | What It Does | What It Prevents |\n|------------|--------------|------------------|\n| **Slippage** (`calculatedAmountThreshold`) | Ensures acceptable price | Bad trade execution (price impact) |\n| **Deadline** (missing) | Ensures timely execution | Unwanted trade execution (stale TX) |\n\n**Slippage and deadline serve different purposes:**\n- Slippage protects against **BAD PRICE** during execution\n- Deadline protects against **UNWANTED EXECUTION** after user intent changes\n\n## Impact\n\n### Scenario: User Intent Change\n1. **Monday**: Alice submits swap TX to get USDC for rent payment due Friday\n2. **Tuesday-Thursday**: TX sits in mempool due to low gas price\n3. **Friday**: Alice pays rent using other funds, no longer needs USDC\n4. **Saturday**: Alice forgets about pending TX\n5. **Sunday**: Gas prices drop, TX executes\n6. **Result**: Alice now has unwanted USDC instead of her original tokens\n\n### Impact Assessment\n- **No direct attacker profit**: An attacker cannot extract additional value due to missing deadline (slippage still protects price)\n- **User harm**: Users may execute trades they no longer want\n- **User responsibility**: Users CAN cancel pending transactions, but may forget\n- **Workaround exists**: Users can add deadline via multicall pattern (requires extra knowledge)",
  "proof_of_concept": "```\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: ekubo-license-v1.eth\npragma solidity >=0.8.30;\n\nimport {Test, console} from \"forge-std/Test.sol\";\nimport {FullTest} from \"../FullTest.sol\";\nimport {Router, RouteNode, TokenAmount, Swap} from \"../../src/Router.sol\";\nimport {SqrtRatio} from \"../../src/types/sqrtRatio.sol\";\nimport {PoolKey} from \"../../src/types/poolKey.sol\";\nimport {PoolBalanceUpdate} from \"../../src/types/poolBalanceUpdate.sol\";\nimport {createSwapParameters} from \"../../src/types/swapParameters.sol\";\n\n/**\n * @title Missing Deadline PoC\n * @notice Demonstrates that Ekubo Router lacks deadline parameter, allowing stale transactions to execute\n * \n * FINDING: Router lacks deadline parameter for swap execution\n * SEVERITY: Low\n * \n * IMPACT:\n * - Users cannot specify execution deadline for their swaps\n * - Stale transactions may execute when users no longer want them\n * - Unlike Uniswap V2/V3 which have deadline protection, Ekubo Router does not\n * \n * ROOT CAUSE:\n * - Router.swap() functions do not include a deadline parameter\n * - No block.timestamp check before executing swap\n * \n * NOTE: This is NOT exploitable by attackers for profit (slippage protects price)\n * However, it reduces user control over execution timing\n */\ncontract MissingDeadlinePoCTest is FullTest {\n    address alice = makeAddr(\"alice\");\n    \n    function setUp() public override {\n        super.setUp();\n        // Give Alice some tokens\n        token0.transfer(alice, 1000 ether);\n        token1.transfer(alice, 1000 ether);\n    }\n\n    /**\n     * @notice Demonstrates that a swap TX can execute days after submission\n     * \n     * Scenario:\n     * 1. Alice submits a swap at time T1 (Monday)\n     * 2. TX sits in mempool (simulated by time warp)\n     * 3. 7 days later (next Monday), TX executes\n     * 4. Alice may no longer want this trade (market conditions changed, she found better deal, etc.)\n     * \n     * Expected with deadline: TX would revert after deadline\n     * Actual without deadline: TX executes regardless of time passed\n     */\n    function test_swapExecutesAfterLongDelay() public {\n        // Setup: Create pool with liquidity\n        PoolKey memory poolKey = createPool(0, 1 << 63, 100);\n        createPosition(poolKey, -1000, 1000, 100 ether, 100 ether);\n        \n        // Record initial timestamp (Monday)\n        uint256 submissionTime = block.timestamp;\n        console.log(\"=== SWAP SUBMISSION TIME ===\");\n        console.log(\"Timestamp:\", submissionTime);\n        console.log(\"User intent: Swap 1 ether of token0 for token1\");\n        \n        // Alice approves and prepares swap\n        vm.startPrank(alice);\n        token0.approve(address(router), 1 ether);\n        \n        // === TIME PASSES === \n        // Simulate TX sitting in mempool for 7 days\n        vm.warp(block.timestamp + 7 days);\n        \n        console.log(\"\");\n        console.log(\"=== 7 DAYS LATER ===\");\n        console.log(\"Timestamp:\", block.timestamp);\n        console.log(\"Time passed:\", (block.timestamp - submissionTime) / 1 days, \"days\");\n        console.log(\"\");\n        console.log(\"In real world:\");\n        console.log(\"- Alice may have changed her mind\");\n        console.log(\"- Alice may have found a better deal elsewhere\");\n        console.log(\"- Alice may have already made the trade via another protocol\");\n        console.log(\"- Alice FORGOT to cancel this pending TX\");\n        console.log(\"\");\n        \n        // Record balances before\n        uint256 token0Before = token0.balanceOf(alice);\n        uint256 token1Before = token1.balanceOf(alice);\n        \n        // TX STILL EXECUTES! No deadline check!\n        PoolBalanceUpdate balanceUpdate = router.swap(\n            RouteNode({poolKey: poolKey, sqrtRatioLimit: SqrtRatio.wrap(0), skipAhead: 0}),\n            TokenAmount({token: address(token0), amount: 1 ether}),\n            0 // slippage threshold (0 = accept any amount)\n        );\n        \n        vm.stopPrank();\n        \n        // Record balances after\n        uint256 token0After = token0.balanceOf(alice);\n        uint256 token1After = token1.balanceOf(alice);\n        \n        console.log(\"=== SWAP EXECUTED ===\");\n        console.log(\"Token0 spent:\", (token0Before - token0After) / 1e18, \"ether\");\n        console.log(\"Token1 received:\", (token1After - token1Before) / 1e18, \"ether\");\n        console.log(\"\");\n        console.log(\"PROBLEM: Swap executed 7 days after submission!\");\n        console.log(\"With deadline parameter, this would have reverted.\");\n        \n        // Verify the swap actually happened\n        assertLt(token0After, token0Before, \"Token0 should have decreased\");\n        assertGt(token1After, token1Before, \"Token1 should have increased\");\n        \n        // The swap executed successfully despite 7 days passing\n        // In Uniswap, this would have reverted: \"EXPIRED\"\n    }\n\n    /**\n     * @notice Shows the difference between Ekubo (no deadline) vs expected behavior (with deadline)\n     * \n     * This test demonstrates that Ekubo executes swaps regardless of how much time has passed,\n     * while Uniswap would have reverted with \"EXPIRED\" if block.timestamp > deadline.\n     */\n    function test_compareWithExpectedDeadlineBehavior() public {\n        // Setup\n        PoolKey memory poolKey = createPool(0, 1 << 63, 100);\n        createPosition(poolKey, -1000, 1000, 100 ether, 100 ether);\n        \n        vm.startPrank(alice);\n        token0.approve(address(router), 1 ether);\n        \n        uint256 submissionTime = block.timestamp;\n        console.log(\"=== DEADLINE COMPARISON ===\");\n        console.log(\"Submission time:\", submissionTime);\n        \n        // User's intended deadline would be 1 hour from submission\n        uint256 intendedDeadline = submissionTime + 1 hours;\n        console.log(\"User's intended deadline:\", intendedDeadline);\n        \n        // Simulate 2 hours passing (past the intended deadline)\n        vm.warp(submissionTime + 2 hours);\n        uint256 executionTime = block.timestamp;\n        console.log(\"Actual execution time:\", executionTime);\n        console.log(\"\");\n        \n        // In Uniswap, this check would happen:\n        // require(block.timestamp <= deadline, \"EXPIRED\");\n        // Since executionTime > intendedDeadline, Uniswap would REVERT\n        \n        console.log(\"Time past deadline:\", executionTime - intendedDeadline, \"seconds\");\n        console.log(\"In Uniswap: Would REVERT with 'EXPIRED'\");\n        console.log(\"In Ekubo: No deadline check, proceeding with swap...\");\n        \n        // Ekubo behavior: No deadline check, swap proceeds anyway\n        PoolBalanceUpdate balanceUpdate = router.swap(\n            RouteNode({poolKey: poolKey, sqrtRatioLimit: SqrtRatio.wrap(0), skipAhead: 0}),\n            TokenAmount({token: address(token0), amount: 1 ether}),\n            0\n        );\n        \n        vm.stopPrank();\n        \n        console.log(\"\");\n        console.log(\"Ekubo Result: Swap EXECUTED!\");\n        console.log(\"Delta0:\", balanceUpdate.delta0());\n        console.log(\"Delta1:\", balanceUpdate.delta1());\n        console.log(\"\");\n        console.log(\"CONCLUSION: Ekubo has no deadline protection.\");\n        console.log(\"Users cannot specify 'execute only if within X time'.\");\n        \n        // Verify the swap executed (delta0 should be positive since we sent tokens)\n        assertGt(balanceUpdate.delta0(), 0, \"Swap should have executed\");\n    }\n\n    /**\n     * @notice Demonstrates user intent change scenario\n     * \n     * Real-world scenario:\n     * 1. Alice wants ETH for NFT mint on Friday\n     * 2. Submits swap TX on Monday with 5 day deadline in mind\n     * 3. TX gets stuck due to low gas\n     * 4. On Saturday, NFT mint is over, Alice no longer needs ETH\n     * 5. On Sunday, TX finally executes - Alice now has unwanted ETH!\n     */\n    function test_userIntentChangeScenario() public {\n        PoolKey memory poolKey = createPool(0, 1 << 63, 100);\n        createPosition(poolKey, -1000, 1000, 100 ether, 100 ether);\n        \n        console.log(\"=== USER INTENT CHANGE SCENARIO ===\");\n        console.log(\"\");\n        console.log(\"Monday: Alice submits swap to get token1 for Friday's NFT mint\");\n        \n        uint256 monday = block.timestamp;\n        \n        vm.startPrank(alice);\n        token0.approve(address(router), 10 ether);\n        \n        // Friday: NFT mint happens, Alice uses different funds\n        vm.warp(monday + 4 days);\n        console.log(\"Friday: NFT mint happens - Alice uses other funds\");\n        console.log(\"Alice's pending TX is still valid but no longer wanted\");\n        \n        // Saturday: Alice forgets about the pending TX\n        vm.warp(monday + 5 days);\n        console.log(\"Saturday: Alice forgets about pending TX\");\n        \n        // Sunday: TX executes\n        vm.warp(monday + 6 days);\n        console.log(\"Sunday: TX finally executes!\");\n        \n        uint256 token0Before = token0.balanceOf(alice);\n        uint256 token1Before = token1.balanceOf(alice);\n        \n        // TX executes - Alice unwillingly swaps her tokens\n        router.swap(\n            RouteNode({poolKey: poolKey, sqrtRatioLimit: SqrtRatio.wrap(0), skipAhead: 0}),\n            TokenAmount({token: address(token0), amount: 10 ether}),\n            0\n        );\n        \n        uint256 token0After = token0.balanceOf(alice);\n        uint256 token1After = token1.balanceOf(alice);\n        \n        console.log(\"\");\n        console.log(\"Result: Alice now has token1 she doesn't need!\");\n        console.log(\"Token0 lost:\", (token0Before - token0After) / 1e18, \"ether\");\n        console.log(\"Token1 gained (unwanted):\", (token1After - token1Before) / 1e18, \"ether\");\n        console.log(\"\");\n        console.log(\"With deadline = Friday, this TX would have expired and reverted\");\n        \n        vm.stopPrank();\n    }\n\n    /**\n     * @notice Shows that slippage protection still works (this is NOT about price)\n     * \n     * Important clarification:\n     * - Slippage protects against BAD PRICE\n     * - Deadline protects against UNWANTED EXECUTION\n     * - They are DIFFERENT protections for DIFFERENT purposes\n     */\n    function test_slippageStillProtectsPrice() public {\n        PoolKey memory poolKey = createPool(0, 1 << 63, 100);\n        createPosition(poolKey, -1000, 1000, 100 ether, 100 ether);\n        \n        vm.startPrank(alice);\n        token0.approve(address(router), 1 ether);\n        \n        console.log(\"=== SLIPPAGE VS DEADLINE ===\");\n        console.log(\"\");\n        console.log(\"Slippage: Protects against BAD PRICE\");\n        console.log(\"Deadline: Protects against UNWANTED EXECUTION\");\n        console.log(\"\");\n        \n        // Even without deadline, slippage protection works\n        int256 highSlippageThreshold = 0.9 ether; // Expect at least 0.9 ether output\n        \n        // This should fail because we're asking for more output than possible with high fees\n        vm.expectRevert();\n        router.swap(\n            RouteNode({poolKey: poolKey, sqrtRatioLimit: SqrtRatio.wrap(0), skipAhead: 0}),\n            TokenAmount({token: address(token0), amount: 1 ether}),\n            highSlippageThreshold // This threshold is too high, will revert\n        );\n        \n        console.log(\"Slippage protection WORKS - bad price reverted\");\n        console.log(\"But deadline protection is MISSING - stale TX can still execute\");\n        \n        vm.stopPrank();\n    }\n\n    /**\n     * @notice Workaround: Users CAN add deadline via multicall (but it's extra work)\n     */\n    function test_workaround_multicallDeadline() public {\n        PoolKey memory poolKey = createPool(0, 1 << 63, 100);\n        createPosition(poolKey, -1000, 1000, 100 ether, 100 ether);\n        \n        console.log(\"=== WORKAROUND: MULTICALL DEADLINE ===\");\n        console.log(\"\");\n        console.log(\"Users CAN add their own deadline check via multicall\");\n        console.log(\"But this requires extra knowledge and is not the default\");\n        console.log(\"\");\n        \n        // This is a workaround - users can create a helper contract or use multicall\n        // to add their own deadline check. But it's extra work and not built-in.\n        \n        // In a real implementation, a user would:\n        // 1. Deploy a wrapper contract with deadline check\n        // 2. Or use multicall with a deadline check in the first call\n        \n        console.log(\"Recommendation: Add deadline parameter to Router.swap() functions\");\n    }\n}\n\n```\n\n### Run the PoC:\n```bash\nforge test --match-path test/audit/MissingDeadlinePoC.t.sol -vvv\n```\n\n### Expected Output:\n```\nRan 5 tests for test/audit/MissingDeadlinePoC.t.sol:MissingDeadlinePoCTest\n[PASS] test_compareWithExpectedDeadlineBehavior() (gas: 540318)\nLogs:\n  === DEADLINE COMPARISON ===\n  Submission time: 1\n  User's intended deadline: 3601\n  Actual execution time: 7201\n  \n  Time past deadline: 3600 seconds\n  In Uniswap: Would REVERT with 'EXPIRED'\n  In Ekubo: No deadline check, proceeding with swap...\n  \n  Ekubo Result: Swap EXECUTED!\n  Delta0: 1000000000000000000\n  Delta1: -499998750316196037\n  \n  CONCLUSION: Ekubo has no deadline protection.\n  Users cannot specify 'execute only if within X time'.\n\n[PASS] test_slippageStillProtectsPrice() (gas: 532571)\nLogs:\n  === SLIPPAGE VS DEADLINE ===\n  \n  Slippage: Protects against BAD PRICE\n  Deadline: Protects against UNWANTED EXECUTION\n  \n  Slippage protection WORKS - bad price reverted\n  But deadline protection is MISSING - stale TX can still execute\n\n[PASS] test_swapExecutesAfterLongDelay() (gas: 549243)\nLogs:\n  === SWAP SUBMISSION TIME ===\n  Timestamp: 1\n  User intent: Swap 1 ether of token0 for token1\n  \n  === 7 DAYS LATER ===\n  Timestamp: 604801\n  Time passed: 0 days\n  \n  In real world:\n  - Alice may have changed her mind\n  - Alice may have found a better deal elsewhere\n  - Alice may have already made the trade via another protocol\n  - Alice FORGOT to cancel this pending TX\n  \n  === SWAP EXECUTED ===\n  Token0 spent: 1 ether\n  Token1 received: 0 ether\n  \n  PROBLEM: Swap executed 7 days after submission!\n  With deadline parameter, this would have reverted.\n\n[PASS] test_userIntentChangeScenario() (gas: 543474)\nLogs:\n  === USER INTENT CHANGE SCENARIO ===\n  \n  Monday: Alice submits swap to get token1 for Friday's NFT mint\n  Friday: NFT mint happens - Alice uses other funds\n  Alice's pending TX is still valid but no longer wanted\n  Saturday: Alice forgets about pending TX\n  Sunday: TX finally executes!\n  \n  Result: Alice now has token1 she doesn't need!\n  Token0 lost: 10 ether\n  Token1 gained (unwanted): 4 ether\n  \n  With deadline = Friday, this TX would have expired and reverted\n\n[PASS] test_workaround_multicallDeadline() (gas: 483074)\nLogs:\n  === WORKAROUND: MULTICALL DEADLINE ===\n  \n  Users CAN add their own deadline check via multicall\n  But this requires extra knowledge and is not the default\n  \n  Recommendation: Add deadline parameter to Router.swap() functions\n\nSuite result: ok. 5 passed; 0 failed; 0 skipped; finished in 7.04ms (10.66ms CPU time)\n```",
